## What changed

Two files touched:

- **src/limiter.ts** — Implemented the token-bucket algorithm:
  - Private fields `tokens` (initialized to `capacity`) and `last` (initialized to `now()`).
  - `refill()`: computes elapsed seconds since last refill, adds tokens at `refillPerSecond`, caps at `capacity`, advances `last` even when capped.
  - `tryTake(n)`: if `n > capacity` returns `false` with only bookkeeping (no token change); if `n <= 0` returns `true`; otherwise refills, deducts if enough tokens, returns `false` without partial deduction.
  - `get available()`: refills to current time and returns the (possibly fractional) token count.

- **src/limiter.test.ts** — Expanded from 1 placeholder test to 7 tests covering:
  - starts full
  - false when empty + no partial take
  - `n > capacity` false even after time passes
  - continuous fractional refill (500ms → +1 at 2/s)
  - cap at capacity after long idle
  - `available` returns fractional and refills to current time
  - uses injected `now()`

